# Resolve known native vehicle blockers before presentation review

Track known vehicle defects that still prevent complete source-faithful native
vehicle construction. These are implementation blockers, not requests for
manual visual tuning.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Construct vehicle render geometry and rig directly from normalized JSON
  without an FBX import prerequisite.
- [ ] Preserve authored wheel geometry while replacing temporary spherical wheel
  collision assumptions with the exact accepted native tire and suspension
  representation.
- [ ] Translate authored articulated joint semantics for doors, hood, and trunk
  instead of leaving secondary bodies permanently kinematic.
- [ ] Recreate source-backed reflective `spheremap`, glass, wheel, and remaining
  material families without inventing PBR values or fallback textures.
- [ ] Bind all source-backed vehicle material slots so missing presentation is
  explicit and no slot silently falls back to Unreal's default material.
- [ ] Preserve the proven vehicle basis with forward `+X`, right `+Y`, and up
  `+Z` through native construction rather than FBX root rotations or mirrors.
- [ ] Keep vehicle self-collision and source joint policy deterministic and
  verified against normalized physics evidence.
- [ ] Retest steering, braking, suspension, damage, articulated parts, cameras,
  and runtime stability after the native asset path replaces FBX.

## Production publication gate — 2026-09-13

The vehicle workspace itself is no longer blocked on normalized-model evidence:
all 88 standalone vehicle rows now carry verified
`shar.normalized-skeletal-model.v1` payloads with matching bytes and SHA-256.
FBX remains alongside those rows only as explicitly deprecated compatibility
evidence.

A full `prepare-unreal` attempt failed closed before publication because the
previous cached vehicle catalog lacked the newly required `normalized_models`
count and per-vehicle normalized-model rows. That stale workspace has now been
regenerated. The next pipeline run must prove the production-plan transition by
publishing 88 native vehicle construction routes and zero vehicle FBX import
routes. Until that atomic publication succeeds, manual presentation review is
not a useful acceptance gate.

After publication, the remaining vehicle implementation blockers are still the
source-faithful physics and presentation items tracked above: self-collision,
authored articulated joints, final wheel/tire behavior, and unresolved material
families. None should be replaced with visual transform fixes, invented PBR
values, or fallback textures.

## Native route published — 2026-09-13

The production publication gate is now complete. A full `prepare-unreal` run
published 88 native vehicle Skeletal Mesh construction operations from
normalized
JSON and zero vehicle FBX import operations. The native source paths and Unreal
destinations are both unique across all 88 vehicles, and every operation is
ready for `SharVehicleSkeletalAssetToolset`.

The remaining blocker is therefore source-faithful vehicle physics and
presentation, not Skeletal Mesh ingestion. The current published Physics Asset
plan contains 137 source rigs, 1,118 primitives, 87 native-ready rigs, and 50
blocked rigs. Its policy intentionally disables all internal body collisions for
source rigs whose self-collision list is empty and keeps secondary bodies
kinematic until authored articulation joints are translated.

The full regenerated corpus confirms that all 137 collision rigs have empty
self-collision lists. The current disable-all internal-body policy therefore
preserves the authored corpus rather than approximating it.

Physics Objects retain 113 one-degree-of-freedom articulated joints across 31
vehicles. Eighty-two articulated joints use stiffness `0.8` with authored angle
range `0.0` to `1.0`; 31 use stiffness `0.5` with authored angle range `0.0` to
`0.5`. Transporting those exact joint records into the native Physics Asset
plan and constructing their constraints is the next physics implementation
boundary.

